# Large raw trial banks are committed gzipped instead; scripts/unpack_raw.py
# restores them. Manifests hash the UNCOMPRESSED bytes, so nothing in the
# provenance chain is weakened by storing them this way.
data/multiobjective/confirmatory/multiobjective_confirmatory_results.csv

# Raw trial banks that are committed gzipped instead.
#
# The confirmatory bank is 97 MB uncompressed and 5.5 MB gzipped. For one
# commit BOTH were tracked, which made `unpack_raw.py` decorative rather than
# load-bearing: the uncompressed file arrived with the clone, so the restore
# path was never exercised by anyone, and the stale-archive defect recorded in
# study/DEVIATIONS.md could sit in the repository undetected. The archive is
# the committed artifact; the uncompressed file is derived from it.
#
# Earlier history still contains the uncompressed blobs. History is not
# rewritten here, so this saves space going forward only.
data/multiobjective/confirmatory/multiobjective_confirmatory_results.csv
